   "overlays": [],
   "project": "fieldnotes",
   "reply": "`list` follows the ISO-8601 rule, with one caveat about stored data.\n\n- **`fieldnotes/cli.py:21`**: `list` prints `note['created']` as it is stored. It does no date formatting of its own, so it uses no `strftime` and no locale-dependent calls.\n- **`fieldnotes/store.py:24`**: `add` writes `created` with `moment.isoformat()`. The timestamp is in UTC, for example `2026-10-28T14:03:11.123456+00:00`.\n- **Other date output**: `add` prints only the note text. Nothing else in `fieldnotes/` prints a date.\n\nThe caveat is that `list` trusts whatever string is in `notes.json`. A note that was hand-edited or written by another tool in a non-ISO format would be printed unchanged. `store.add` can't produce that, and I didn't check the contents of any existing `notes.json`.\n\nIf you want a guarantee, `list` could parse each value with `datetime.fromisoformat` and re-emit it. I haven't changed anything.",
   "suspended": false
