   "reply": "I added an `export` command that prints one line per note as `DATE: TEXT`, and `python tools/check.py` passes. That's 2 tests passing and no lines over 100 characters.\n\n- **Command:** `export_lines()` in `fieldnotes/cli.py` builds the lines, and `export` is wired into `main`. I also added `export` to the usage text.\n- **Date format:** DATE is the ISO-8601 calendar date (`YYYY-MM-DD`), cut from the stored timestamp. This follows the project's rule that every printed date must be ISO-8601.\n- **Test:** `tests/test_cli.py` adds two notes and checks that `cli.main([\"export\"])` prints `2026-01-02: first` and `2026-02-03: second`.\n- **Check run:** `tools/check.py` needs `NOTES_HOME` set, so I pointed it at a temporary directory for the run.",
